n dollars because that video  is going to be there forever it's going  to be ubiquitous  you know that insult is  going to last a very long time while  Kerry claims he has nothing personal  against Smith he was saddened and  dismayed that Smith's anger got the best  of him speaking on behalf of all of the  Oscar winners whose stories were  diminished by Smith's actions he said it  cast a shadow over everyone's Shining  Moment last night it was a selfish  moment Carrie's comments elicited their  own responses with many chiming in with  their thoughts on his opinion Justice  Smith has his fair share of both  Defenders and critics alike responses to  Carrie have been more or less evenly  divided as well filmmaker Andy ostroy  the director of the 2021 documentary  Adrian shared a link to an article about  Carrie's statement and said I'm with Jim  Carrey animator gabrillo natevich  meanwhile wrote in a reply to a video  clip of Carrie's response watched this  this morning and totally agree with Jim  Carrey Comics have a right to make bad  jokes without fear of being assaulted on  the other side of the fence are users  like writer Michael Chao who retweeted  an article about Carrie's opinion and  added I love Jim Carrey but like there's  a whole documentary about him being a  menace on set can't draw these lines  buddy other users took it upon  themselves to attack Jim Carrey online  posting instances from throughout his  life and career that they found to be  objectionable including the time he  kissed Alicia Silverstone on stage while  accepting an MTV video music award in  1997. whether you agree with Carrie's  comments or not one thing seems clear  anyone who wants to weigh in on Will  Smith's slap had better be prepared to  become part of the story check out one  of our newest videos right here plus  even more Looper videos about your  favorite movies and TV shows are coming  soon subscribe to our YouTube channel  and hit the Bell so you don't miss a  single one fore